From 310ad829b8637a77661ed0f4f6b50a8c2487a0ab Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Muhammad Hassaan Shaukat <mr.hassaan50@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 18:15:12 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 05/10] Derive every reported number from the run artifacts in
 one place

The report's statistics had been transcribed, which is how a sentence saying "P vs V
changes only the channel" reached a draft when no such pair of arms exists. This module
is the only allowed source of figures: it pins the artifact each arm reads from, refuses
a run whose recorded turns carry an error payload, and derives the comparisons the prose
makes rather than restating them.

The matched-ladder claim is now checked against the whole YAML document, not a hand-picked
subset of keys. Both config trees are flattened to leaf values and diffed, and the build
raises if anything moves outside the arm's own naming fields and the four intervention
keys. That found real differences nobody had listed: coalition_prompt, observation_filter,
prompt_variants and secret_channel_enabled are what separate the seven arms, and nothing
else does.

It also computes the things a reader should be able to audit: the single-seed noise floor
from the re-run of arm E, the one pair of arms differing only in the coalition prompt,
the absence of any pair differing only in the secret channel, and the accounting closure
of both offline harnesses. Running the module prints the whole map.
